From dbafd291a3d4d1ff2b4338ba1ee0cc8c65224277 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:33:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: Shoot'N'Scoot reads the danger of the adjacent monster

borg_shoot_scoot_safe() scans the eight grids around the Borg for an
awake monster worth phasing away from.  One of its tests compares that
monster's danger with the Borg's hit points, but it passed the loop's
direction number (0-7) to borg_danger_one_kill() instead of the kill
index of the monster standing in that grid.  The test therefore read
whatever monster happened to occupy kill slot 0-7, which may be far
away and out of sight, and could make the Borg cast Phase Door to get
away from a weak neighbour it would not shoot at.

Pass ag->kill, the index of the adjacent monster.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#100.
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
index 0c347c5ad..57d58293b 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
@@ -2973,7 +2973,7 @@ bool borg_shoot_scoot_safe(int emergency, int turns, int b_p)
              * list in borg_launch_damage_one()
              */
             else if ((borg_danger_one_kill(
-                          kill->pos.y, kill->pos.x, 1, i, true, false)
+                          kill->pos.y, kill->pos.x, 1, ag->kill, true, false)
                          > borg.avoidance * 3 / 10)
                      || ((r_ptr->friends
                              || r_ptr->friends_base) /* monster has friends*/
